# Line endings are per-file, not per-checkout.
#
# core.autocrlf rewrites working-tree files on checkout, which turns a shell
# script into one Linux cannot run ("bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M").
# The scripts here are part of the build and the release, so their endings are
# stated rather than guessed at.

* text=auto

*.sh text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Fixtures are byte-exact: several tests compare whole files, and a PDF whose
# newlines were "helpfully" converted is a different document with a different
# xref table.
*.pdf binary
*.docx binary
*.dll binary
*.so binary
*.dylib binary
